// Scripts share the REPL's prelude (ADR-42): operators and module builtins
// resolve inside a shell-mode program, so a script can COMPUTE over a
// command's reply instead of merely relaying it. (This pins the wyrd-4eys
// regression, where the prelude was absent from the shell state and every
// operator use in a script stuck on `forced non-thunk`.)
//
// The reply of a `#!{ ... }` block is a record (13-shell-blocks); this
// script binds the reply, then decides a typed fact about the captured
// stdout with a string builtin. Predicates return `Bool = 1 + 1`, so the
// hit renders as the annotated `Inl(())`.
{
  run banner <- #!{ printf 'hello from gandr\n'; };
  string.contains(banner.stdout, "gandr")
}

// The harness checks:
//@ mode: shell
//@ expect-shell-value: Inl(())
